From 43943371af5f59bdbfdaf4e9722ac314af06a489 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: austin62jake <340374338+austin62jake@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:51:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app): verify's ok is false while an op's own warnings
 hold the post (#722)

v_verify (cam.verify, cam.check, the MCP verify tool, and through them the
camcraft-cli process exit code) said ok: true for a fresh program whose
gate passed even when an op's cached warnings blocked the post, so the
post then refused with "post blocked - N warning(s)" and the CLI exited 0.
ok now also requires that no in-scope, non-suppressed op holds a warning
that blocks_post(), the same rule posting::stream_records applies, and the
report names those ops under held_by (typed in cam.d.ts).

Pinned by crates/app/tests/mcp_verify.rs: a 30 mm contour with
EM-0400-2FL (its shank rubs below the 12 mm flutes) verifies not ok, names
C1 and still refuses to post; the 10 mm neighbour stays ok and posts; the
CLI process lane exits 1 and 0 for them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
